# Each word sells a feature instead of describing it. `first class`
# and `super` are left out, because each names something in code (a
# first-class function, a superclass call). `enduring` stays out too
# (`enduring storage outlives the pod`).
#
# Two words keep a technical sense behind a guard. `robust to` names a
# statistical property (`robust to outliers`), and `highly available`
# names a deployment shape. A negated word after a space needs a word
# to consume, so `robust` has a twin for a clause end (`robust!( )`).
#
# A space in a pattern matches only whitespace, so each compound that
# writers also hyphenate takes `[-, ( )]` between its words and
# matches `battle tested` and `battle-tested` alike.
expr main [seamless, seamlessly, (robust !to), (robust!( )), powerful, elegant, elegantly, comprehensive, intuitive, effortless, effortlessly, blazing, blazingly, revolutionary, innovative, sophisticated, intricate, vibrant, (a breeze), holistic, groundbreaking, transformative, (ever[-, ( )]evolving), (rapidly evolving), (top[-, ( )]notch), (battle[-, ( )]tested), (production[-, ( )]ready), (enterprise[-, ( )]grade), (out[-, ( )]of[-, ( )]the[-, ( )]box), (bells and whistles), (feature[-, ( )]rich), (cutting[-, ( )]edge), (state[-, ( )]of[-, ( )]the[-, ( )]art), (lightning[-, ( )]fast), (best[-, ( )]in[-, ( )]class), (world[-, ( )]class), (next[-, ( )]generation), (game[-, ( )]changing), (highly !available)]
let message "Puff. State the fact and let the reader judge its weight."
let description "Flags marketing adjectives that inflate a claim without informing."
let becomes ""
let kind "Style"
allows "The bucket refills every second."
allows "The estimator is robust to outliers."
allows "The cluster is highly available."
allows "Go has first-class functions."
